@startuml
title Figure 5.5: Sequence Diagram of the Automated Coverage Analysis (component level).
participant "Vue\n(Coverage.vue)" as Vue
participant "Rust Core\n(coverage.rs)" as Rust
participant "coverage.py" as Cov
database "SQLite" as DB
entity "coverage.json" as JSON

note over Vue: triggered manually or via ?autoRun=1 (one-click after execution)
Vue -> Rust: run_coverage(projectId, path, ...)
Rust -> Cov: coverage erase
Rust -> Cov: coverage run --branch -m pytest
Rust -> Cov: coverage json -o coverage.json
Cov --> Rust: status
Rust -> JSON: write coverage.json + meta.json
Rust -> Rust: parse JSON (format 1/2)
Rust --> Vue: event coverage-finished {summary}
Rust -> DB: save coverage_results + coverage_history

Vue -> Rust: get_coverage_detail(filePath)
Rust -> JSON: read coverage.json + source
Rust --> Vue: line-level four-state data
Vue -> Vue: render highlighted code viewer
@enduml
